23:    - Below it is a one-cell-thick rectangular frame around a black interior.
24:    - Non-black, non-frame interior pixels are marker colors; one marker color has
25:      the unique highest count.
26:
27:    Rule:
28:    - Keep the palette row unchanged.
29:    - Pick the uniquely most frequent interior marker color.
30:    - Clear the lower board to black, recolor its outer frame with the picked color,
31:      and draw the picked color's interior bounding-box border.
32:
33:    Key insight:
34:    - The noisy marker cloud is not preserved as pixels; only the majority marker
35:      color and its spatial extent define the output.
36:    """
37:    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
38:    assert g.ndim == 2, "expected a 2D grid"
